WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.194 --> 00:00:04.136
- Hello Believe Nation.

00:00:04.136 --> 00:00:06.598
Today I'm going to talk
about seven effective ways

00:00:06.598 --> 00:00:08.542
to beat stress.

00:00:08.542 --> 00:00:10.481
And as always guys, if you
hear a point that really

00:00:10.481 --> 00:00:12.942
resonates with you please
leave it down, comments below,

00:00:12.942 --> 00:00:14.223
put quotes around it so other people

00:00:14.223 --> 00:00:15.681
can be inspired as well.

00:00:15.681 --> 00:00:17.590
And also writing it
down, helps you lock it

00:00:17.590 --> 00:00:19.200
in for yourself too.

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:20.462
Enjoy.

00:00:20.462 --> 00:00:23.311
- [Announcer] Nine, eight.

00:00:23.311 --> 00:00:25.894
(upbeat music)

00:00:27.978 --> 00:00:29.572
- So being an entrepreneur
is one of the most stressful

00:00:29.572 --> 00:00:31.107
things I think you can do in your life.

00:00:31.107 --> 00:00:33.023
It's going to be one of the hardest things

00:00:33.023 --> 00:00:35.505
you will ever do in your
life, is to start a business.

00:00:35.505 --> 00:00:36.795
I don't think enough people talk about

00:00:36.795 --> 00:00:38.786
the difficulties associated with it.

00:00:38.786 --> 00:00:41.694
There's a reason why 80 to
90 percent of companies fail.

00:00:41.694 --> 00:00:44.347
Because it's stressful,
because it's hard, it sucks.

00:00:44.347 --> 00:00:46.123
There's a lot that goes
into building a company

00:00:46.123 --> 00:00:48.156
that we just don't talk enough about

00:00:48.156 --> 00:00:50.477
and I think entrepreneurs are
among the most stressed out

00:00:50.477 --> 00:00:51.638
people in the world.

00:00:51.638 --> 00:00:53.850
And listen, we're trying
to do big, bold, empowering

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:56.288
exciting things and so I'm
going to share with you

00:00:56.288 --> 00:00:58.337
seven ways that I hope
will effectively beat

00:00:58.337 --> 00:00:59.441
the stress for you.

00:00:59.441 --> 00:01:01.122
Some of them are things
you can do immediately.

00:01:01.122 --> 00:01:02.981
Some of the things that will
work over a longer period

00:01:02.981 --> 00:01:05.403
of time as well and I
hope you enjoy the video.

00:01:05.403 --> 00:01:07.986
(upbeat music)

00:01:09.025 --> 00:01:12.479
So way number one is ask
yourself does this matter?

00:01:12.479 --> 00:01:15.037
It's surprising how much
of the stuff that we put

00:01:15.037 --> 00:01:19.954
on our plate every single
day, doesn't actually matter.

00:01:19.954 --> 00:01:21.813
And the things that we stress about

00:01:21.813 --> 00:01:24.419
are so little and so tiny
that in the big picture

00:01:24.419 --> 00:01:26.079
they don't actually matter.

00:01:26.079 --> 00:01:28.182
So when you're in the stressful zone

00:01:28.182 --> 00:01:30.632
the hardest thing to
do is just step outside

00:01:30.632 --> 00:01:32.402
and look at yourself.

00:01:32.402 --> 00:01:34.775
Look at yourself and say,
that thing that I'm worrying

00:01:34.775 --> 00:01:37.499
about does that actually
matter and more often that not,

00:01:37.499 --> 00:01:39.157
you'll come back with a no.

00:01:39.157 --> 00:01:41.086
Like, this actually doesn't
matter and I'm being stressed

00:01:41.086 --> 00:01:43.200
out for no reason and
it's going to work out

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:44.196
in the big picture.

00:01:44.196 --> 00:01:46.687
So as an example, I have
mastermind groups in Toronto

00:01:46.687 --> 00:01:49.394
and I used to keep meeting
minutes and I used to keep notes

00:01:49.394 --> 00:01:51.489
on what happened in the
meetings and I would email it

00:01:51.489 --> 00:01:53.080
to everybody after each session.

00:01:53.080 --> 00:01:55.228
It took me a while to
put the notes together,

00:01:55.228 --> 00:01:57.452
a summary, I thought it was
a value wide service right?

00:01:57.452 --> 00:01:59.288
Evan keeps preaching add
value, I thought this

00:01:59.288 --> 00:02:01.343
was adding a lot of
value to people's lives

00:02:01.343 --> 00:02:03.353
and it would stress me
out always to take notes

00:02:03.353 --> 00:02:06.218
as quick as I could and
then send it off to people

00:02:06.218 --> 00:02:07.314
as fast as I could.

00:02:07.314 --> 00:02:10.919
And there was time then when
I just didn't have the time.

00:02:10.919 --> 00:02:12.693
I was stressed out, I had
too much stuff happening,

00:02:12.693 --> 00:02:15.215
I didn't have the time to
send notes out to people.

00:02:15.215 --> 00:02:17.015
And you know what happened?

00:02:17.015 --> 00:02:18.046
Nothing.

00:02:18.046 --> 00:02:19.238
Nothing happened.

00:02:19.238 --> 00:02:20.450
Nobody cared.

00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:22.326
Nobody wrote to me and
said where the notes,

00:02:22.326 --> 00:02:23.438
where are the minutes?

00:02:23.438 --> 00:02:26.315
And then the next month I didn't
do it again, nobody cared.

00:02:26.315 --> 00:02:29.687
I was doing all this work
and stressing myself out

00:02:29.687 --> 00:02:31.665
over something that didn't matter.

00:02:31.665 --> 00:02:33.077
Nobody actually cared about it.

00:02:33.077 --> 00:02:34.853
I convinced myself that it was important

00:02:34.853 --> 00:02:36.943
but it actually wasn't important.

00:02:36.943 --> 00:02:38.143
And so thinking about the things

00:02:38.143 --> 00:02:41.249
that stress you out, how
much are they really part

00:02:41.249 --> 00:02:44.403
of the big picture, where
you see yourself going,

00:02:44.403 --> 00:02:47.241
does this thing actually really matter.

00:02:47.241 --> 00:02:49.215
Usually it's no and just that awareness,

00:02:49.215 --> 00:02:51.390
just asking that question
can immediately help

00:02:51.390 --> 00:02:52.674
reduce the stress.

00:02:52.674 --> 00:02:55.821
(upbeat music)

00:02:55.821 --> 00:02:57.829
Way number two to
effectively reduce stress

00:02:57.829 --> 00:02:59.313
is come back to it tomorrow.

00:02:59.313 --> 00:03:01.236
Sometimes I find that if I'm in the moment

00:03:01.236 --> 00:03:03.431
and I'm stressed out and
I'm angry or agitated

00:03:03.431 --> 00:03:05.903
and I'm not thinking clearly.

00:03:05.903 --> 00:03:07.550
Sometimes the best thing to do

00:03:07.550 --> 00:03:10.537
is just to leave it, go to something else,

00:03:10.537 --> 00:03:11.934
and come back to it the next day.

00:03:11.934 --> 00:03:13.461
And the next day to come back to it,

00:03:13.461 --> 00:03:15.585
when your mind is fresh
and you're in a different

00:03:15.585 --> 00:03:18.885
head space and the answer comes to you.

00:03:18.885 --> 00:03:20.800
And so I find that if I'm
ever struggling on something,

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:23.347
I just, I'm not getting through,
I'm not getting an answer.

00:03:23.347 --> 00:03:24.660
Just push it off.

00:03:24.660 --> 00:03:26.135
It's not like push it off forever,

00:03:26.135 --> 00:03:28.514
unless it's not important,
but coming back to it the next

00:03:28.514 --> 00:03:31.771
day, I find often I come with a solution

00:03:31.771 --> 00:03:34.705
that comes super fast and
I just saved a lot of time

00:03:34.705 --> 00:03:36.614
because I wasn't spending
hours and hours and hours

00:03:36.614 --> 00:03:38.508
frustrated trying to figure out a problem.

00:03:38.508 --> 00:03:41.091
(upbeat music)

00:03:42.142 --> 00:03:45.003
Way number three to reduce
stress is finish it now.

00:03:45.003 --> 00:03:47.938
This may seem counter
intuitive and the opposite

00:03:47.938 --> 00:03:50.396
of what I just talked about
in finish it tomorrow.

00:03:50.396 --> 00:03:53.868
And I think the context really
is if you have an answer.

00:03:53.868 --> 00:03:56.589
So if I'm stressed out
but I know what to do,

00:03:56.589 --> 00:04:00.125
then I will find it easier
to get it done right now.

00:04:00.125 --> 00:04:02.180
If I don't know what to
do, if I'm frustrated

00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:04.234
and stressed because I
don't have an answer,

00:04:04.234 --> 00:04:05.936
then you can leave it for the next day.

00:04:05.936 --> 00:04:07.666
And so if you have a clear
answer, you know what needs

00:04:07.666 --> 00:04:09.570
to get down and you're
just up against a deadline,

00:04:09.570 --> 00:04:10.801
just get it done.

00:04:10.801 --> 00:04:13.294
What I'll find is, if I
know what needs to get done,

00:04:13.294 --> 00:04:15.410
and I'm delaying it and
I'm waiting till tomorrow

00:04:15.410 --> 00:04:17.794
then I'm spending all that time
thinking about, like I just

00:04:17.794 --> 00:04:19.223
need to get this done, I
just need to get this done.

00:04:19.223 --> 00:04:20.866
And then you're not enjoying
the rest of your day.

00:04:20.866 --> 00:04:22.759
You're not present in any
of your other meetings

00:04:22.759 --> 00:04:24.553
or at home with your
family, you're just always

00:04:24.553 --> 00:04:26.113
just stressed out thinking about it.

00:04:26.113 --> 00:04:28.088
So if you have a clear solution

00:04:28.088 --> 00:04:30.277
then deal with it immediately.

00:04:30.277 --> 00:04:33.069
If you don't know what to
do next, then you can wait.

00:04:33.069 --> 00:04:34.827
Push it off till tomorrow,
come back when you have

00:04:34.827 --> 00:04:35.791
a fresh mind.

00:04:35.791 --> 00:04:38.374
(upbeat music)

00:04:39.361 --> 00:04:41.196
Win number four is model success.

00:04:41.196 --> 00:04:43.611
One of the things that really
helped me in my first business

00:04:43.611 --> 00:04:47.512
got me through the most
stressful part of my life really

00:04:47.512 --> 00:04:49.833
was understanding that I
wasn't the first person

00:04:49.833 --> 00:04:52.089
to try to solve this problem before.

00:04:52.089 --> 00:04:54.181
Now when I told my business
partner that I quit

00:04:54.181 --> 00:04:56.840
and I wanted to leave the
company and then hearing me

00:04:56.840 --> 00:05:00.009
say those words just stressed
me out and I knew the next day

00:05:00.009 --> 00:05:01.610
that I had to go back and do this.

00:05:01.610 --> 00:05:04.380
I couldn't quit on this, I had
to find a way to keep going.

00:05:04.380 --> 00:05:06.289
But I had to find a
different way to stand.

00:05:06.289 --> 00:05:08.878
And the realization of
hitting rock bottom,

00:05:08.878 --> 00:05:10.252
the realization that come to me

00:05:10.252 --> 00:05:12.349
was that somebody else had
figured this out before.

00:05:12.349 --> 00:05:14.580
Whatever thing you're
stressed out about right now,

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:17.246
whatever problem you're faced
and it seems insurmountable

00:05:17.246 --> 00:05:19.668
that it's impossible to overcome,

00:05:19.668 --> 00:05:21.895
many many many people have
already figured it out.

00:05:21.895 --> 00:05:23.219
Many people.

00:05:23.219 --> 00:05:25.768
It's one of the founding
reasons for why I created

00:05:25.768 --> 00:05:27.092
this Youtube channel.

00:05:27.092 --> 00:05:30.081
Was to share the strategies
of successful entrepreneurs.

00:05:30.081 --> 00:05:31.410
And it's from two angles.

00:05:31.410 --> 00:05:33.383
One, the strategy, what do I do?

00:05:33.383 --> 00:05:35.926
I'm facing this problem,
here's a solution.

00:05:35.926 --> 00:05:37.754
Every time I watch one
of the top ten videos,

00:05:37.754 --> 00:05:39.762
or meant to be videos,
or Believe Life videos,

00:05:39.762 --> 00:05:41.708
I learn something, I learn a new strategy

00:05:41.708 --> 00:05:44.095
that I can apply to my
life and to my business.

00:05:44.095 --> 00:05:46.092
Even if I've heard it
before, sometimes it comes

00:05:46.092 --> 00:05:47.652
from a different voice, a different angle,

00:05:47.652 --> 00:05:50.107
and I see it a slightly different
way then I can apply it.

00:05:50.107 --> 00:05:51.990
The second thing it does
though, it also gives you

00:05:51.990 --> 00:05:53.606
just motivation.

00:05:53.606 --> 00:05:55.806
Just for me knowing that
I'm not the only person

00:05:55.806 --> 00:05:58.656
in the world who's ever gone through this.

00:05:58.656 --> 00:06:02.511
Seeing other entrepreneurs
have hard times and fail

00:06:02.511 --> 00:06:05.615
and struggle, made me
feel like this is normal.

00:06:05.615 --> 00:06:07.642
What I'm dealing with is normal.

00:06:07.642 --> 00:06:10.446
If they can through it, then
I can get through it too.

00:06:10.446 --> 00:06:13.204
A lot of these people started with less

00:06:13.204 --> 00:06:15.523
than what you already have right now.

00:06:15.523 --> 00:06:17.913
You already have more
money, more resources,

00:06:17.913 --> 00:06:20.464
more connections, more
opportunities than a lot

00:06:20.464 --> 00:06:23.058
of these successful entrepreneurs
had when they started.

00:06:23.058 --> 00:06:26.089
You're starting with
more than what they had.

00:06:26.089 --> 00:06:28.109
And so I would tell myself,
listen if they could do it,

00:06:28.109 --> 00:06:29.021
why can't I?

00:06:29.021 --> 00:06:31.476
They don't have any natural advantage.

00:06:31.476 --> 00:06:33.542
If they can do it, I can get it too.

00:06:33.542 --> 00:06:35.677
And so by modeling
success, one to figure out

00:06:35.677 --> 00:06:38.899
the specific strategies and
tactics, things that I can apply

00:06:38.899 --> 00:06:40.956
but also just the motivation
to know that these

00:06:40.956 --> 00:06:43.747
successful people went
through the same thing I was.

00:06:43.747 --> 00:06:45.640
That dramatically helped
me reduce my stress.

00:06:45.640 --> 00:06:48.223
(upbeat music)

00:06:49.112 --> 00:06:52.401
Number five is join or
start a mastermind group.

00:06:52.401 --> 00:06:53.965
I think one of the biggest
challenges of being

00:06:53.965 --> 00:06:55.904
an entrepreneur is that you're alone.

00:06:55.904 --> 00:06:57.877
You don't have other
entrepreneurs to talk to.

00:06:57.877 --> 00:07:00.071
So many entrepreneurs that
I connect with and meet,

00:07:00.071 --> 00:07:02.794
they're the only
entrepreneurs in their circle.

00:07:02.794 --> 00:07:04.325
Their family, they're not entrepreneurs.

00:07:04.325 --> 00:07:05.823
Their friends are not entrepreneurs.

00:07:05.823 --> 00:07:07.525
Everybody's telling
them that they're crazy,

00:07:07.525 --> 00:07:09.853
they should do the safe
thing and stay with their job

00:07:09.853 --> 00:07:12.492
or they should take a professional career.

00:07:12.492 --> 00:07:14.903
And sometimes, you know
those people around you

00:07:14.903 --> 00:07:17.637
are hating on you but sometimes
it's just out of love.

00:07:17.637 --> 00:07:21.026
The way that they see
success is a normal typical

00:07:21.026 --> 00:07:23.750
corporate career and
that's not what you want.

00:07:23.750 --> 00:07:25.828
And so when you don't
have people around you

00:07:25.828 --> 00:07:27.991
who are like minded in that capacity,

00:07:27.991 --> 00:07:30.008
it could be really hard to move forward

00:07:30.008 --> 00:07:31.772
and it's easy to get stressed out.

00:07:31.772 --> 00:07:34.163
And so I find that being a
part of a mastermind group,

00:07:34.163 --> 00:07:35.951
if there's one in your
area or you could join

00:07:35.951 --> 00:07:38.094
an online one, we have an online one,

00:07:38.094 --> 00:07:40.190
or you could start your own.

00:07:40.190 --> 00:07:42.477
When you're connecting
with like minded people,

00:07:42.477 --> 00:07:44.108
a lot of the people in my group call it

00:07:44.108 --> 00:07:47.231
entrepreneurs anonymous because half of it

00:07:47.231 --> 00:07:49.704
is about strategies and
tactics, here's the problem

00:07:49.704 --> 00:07:52.142
I'm facing, what do you guys
think, do you have connections

00:07:52.142 --> 00:07:55.241
or ideas to help me and half
of it is just about having

00:07:55.241 --> 00:07:58.835
people around you who understand you.

00:07:58.835 --> 00:08:00.593
Coming to a monthly meeting
where you're connected

00:08:00.593 --> 00:08:02.887
to people who get what
you're going through,

00:08:02.887 --> 00:08:04.848
who've gone through it, who
are facing some of the same

00:08:04.848 --> 00:08:07.270
challenges and just
that emotional support.

00:08:07.270 --> 00:08:09.099
So being a part of a mastermind group,

00:08:09.099 --> 00:08:11.688
again from the strategies
and from the emotional side

00:08:11.688 --> 00:08:13.911
can dramatically help reduce your stress.

00:08:13.911 --> 00:08:16.494
(upbeat music)

00:08:17.498 --> 00:08:19.645
the sixth way to reduce
your stress is to create

00:08:19.645 --> 00:08:21.304
a better schedule.

00:08:21.304 --> 00:08:22.930
I live and die by my schedule.

00:08:22.930 --> 00:08:26.786
I find that if I don't
have it scheduled in

00:08:26.786 --> 00:08:28.772
and I don't have a plot
somewhere in my week

00:08:28.772 --> 00:08:30.403
to deal with something,
then I get stressed out.

00:08:30.403 --> 00:08:31.730
I get antsy, I get nervous.

00:08:31.730 --> 00:08:34.455
Like, when am I going to do
it, I force myself to do it now

00:08:34.455 --> 00:08:37.143
and it may not always be
the best time to do it.

00:08:37.143 --> 00:08:41.350
This happens maybe once
a quarter on a big scale.

00:08:41.350 --> 00:08:43.247
Maybe once a month on a smaller scale

00:08:43.247 --> 00:08:45.930
where just something happens in my life

00:08:45.930 --> 00:08:48.286
or in my business or just I
want to grow and I want to

00:08:48.286 --> 00:08:50.876
learn something else and
to do it I need to take

00:08:50.876 --> 00:08:52.338
time from somewhere else.

00:08:52.338 --> 00:08:54.352
I recognize your time is
limited, you only have

00:08:54.352 --> 00:08:55.846
so many hours in a week.

00:08:55.846 --> 00:08:57.921
You have other interests as well

00:08:57.921 --> 00:08:59.297
and so if you want to add something to it,

00:08:59.297 --> 00:09:00.609
you have to take something away.

00:09:00.609 --> 00:09:02.801
When I took over Toronto
Dance Salsa and acquired

00:09:02.801 --> 00:09:05.508
the business last year,
I knew it would take up

00:09:05.508 --> 00:09:07.068
a lot of my time.

00:09:07.068 --> 00:09:09.193
And so I had to dedicate
a single day in the week.

00:09:09.193 --> 00:09:11.103
So Tuesdays is my Toronto Dance Salsa day,

00:09:11.103 --> 00:09:13.333
all day I'm working on TDS
stuff, I'm working with Alex,

00:09:13.333 --> 00:09:15.271
I'm mentoring, I'm training,
doing all this stuff

00:09:15.271 --> 00:09:17.612
that needs to get done to
build and grow this business.

00:09:17.612 --> 00:09:20.748
It also means that I'm
out three nights a week

00:09:20.748 --> 00:09:24.638
in coming to class, in having
meetings, and going to parties

00:09:24.638 --> 00:09:26.598
and entertaining and hosting.

00:09:26.598 --> 00:09:28.061
So it's a big time commitment that I need

00:09:28.061 --> 00:09:29.408
to be prepared for.

00:09:29.408 --> 00:09:31.848
So one it was talking to my wife Nina

00:09:31.848 --> 00:09:33.566
and saying here's what
I'm thinking of doing

00:09:33.566 --> 00:09:35.377
and getting her support
that this is something

00:09:35.377 --> 00:09:39.429
that I'm committed to and two,
in order for me to free up

00:09:39.429 --> 00:09:42.610
the Tuesday, I had other
stuff planned on that Tuesday.

00:09:42.610 --> 00:09:43.980
But I had to take away some other things

00:09:43.980 --> 00:09:46.802
and say you know, this is
not as important a priority.

00:09:46.802 --> 00:09:49.559
And I think too many times
we just jam our schedule

00:09:49.559 --> 00:09:52.879
or we don't have any kind
of plan for a schedule.

00:09:52.879 --> 00:09:54.480
We just get it filled up with things

00:09:54.480 --> 00:09:56.668
and then when you want to
add something new to it,

00:09:56.668 --> 00:10:00.885
you can't because it's jammed
full and so whenever I feel

00:10:00.885 --> 00:10:04.326
stressed out about something
and it's consistent,

00:10:04.326 --> 00:10:06.584
like every week I'm feeling
stressed out about something,

00:10:06.584 --> 00:10:10.351
I know that I need to make
more time for it in my calendar

00:10:10.351 --> 00:10:12.640
and see if I can find a
way to schedule that in

00:10:12.640 --> 00:10:14.898
so that I will be less
stressed every week.

00:10:14.898 --> 00:10:17.481
(upbeat music)

00:10:18.485 --> 00:10:21.008
And then number seven
effective way to beat stress

00:10:21.008 --> 00:10:22.537
is to get some help.

00:10:22.537 --> 00:10:25.827
You can't do everything
yourself, in your business,

00:10:25.827 --> 00:10:28.731
and you're likely doing things
that you shouldn't be doing.

00:10:28.731 --> 00:10:31.454
And so I mentioned earlier
on that I used to take

00:10:31.454 --> 00:10:33.264
meeting notes and it wasn't effective

00:10:33.264 --> 00:10:35.555
and I should've stopped
doing that a lot earlier.

00:10:35.555 --> 00:10:37.183
That's not something that
you want to get help on,

00:10:37.183 --> 00:10:38.809
that's just something
you want to eliminate.

00:10:38.809 --> 00:10:40.270
First rule is eliminate.

00:10:40.270 --> 00:10:41.467
Look at where you're spending your time

00:10:41.467 --> 00:10:44.225
and eliminate the things
that are not adding

00:10:44.225 --> 00:10:45.221
the most value.

00:10:45.221 --> 00:10:46.830
When you're especially at the
early stage of the business

00:10:46.830 --> 00:10:50.047
and everything is new, you
need to really focus your time

00:10:50.047 --> 00:10:51.364
because you're everything from the CEO

00:10:51.364 --> 00:10:54.169
to the janitor in your business
and so, you need to make

00:10:54.169 --> 00:10:56.745
sure that the time you're
spending is having the most

00:10:56.745 --> 00:10:59.368
impact possible and you're
eliminating the things

00:10:59.368 --> 00:11:01.114
you don't want to be great at.

00:11:01.114 --> 00:11:02.542
So eliminate is number one.

00:11:02.542 --> 00:11:03.738
Automate is number two.

00:11:03.738 --> 00:11:05.333
Look at the task that you're doing,

00:11:05.333 --> 00:11:07.291
if anything is happening consistently

00:11:07.291 --> 00:11:09.514
that should be automated,
you shouldn't go to somebody

00:11:09.514 --> 00:11:11.325
else, it should just be
automated, it should go

00:11:11.325 --> 00:11:15.197
to a software program, a
computer system, a website,

00:11:15.197 --> 00:11:17.838
right, making something so
that there's these tools

00:11:17.838 --> 00:11:20.460
that automate things for you
can really free up your time

00:11:20.460 --> 00:11:23.945
because those tools, they
don't take sick days,

00:11:23.945 --> 00:11:26.522
they don't require vacation
pay, they're a lot lot cheaper

00:11:26.522 --> 00:11:28.485
than having somebody working for you

00:11:28.485 --> 00:11:30.661
and so eliminate is
first, automate is second,

00:11:30.661 --> 00:11:32.391
third is delegate.

00:11:32.391 --> 00:11:34.329
If you're doing something important,

00:11:34.329 --> 00:11:35.538
you have to build a team.

00:11:35.538 --> 00:11:37.883
The first person I hired
was for one hour a day

00:11:37.883 --> 00:11:40.257
and he freed up more than
an hour of my time a day

00:11:40.257 --> 00:11:42.747
because he was better
at the work than I was

00:11:42.747 --> 00:11:45.341
and then I slowly built up my team.

00:11:45.341 --> 00:11:47.547
And so you can hire somebody,
you may not have enough

00:11:47.547 --> 00:11:50.704
money to have somebody come
on full time on your business

00:11:50.704 --> 00:11:52.429
but to hire somebody for an hour a day

00:11:52.429 --> 00:11:54.920
or a couple hours a week to
help take off some of the

00:11:54.920 --> 00:11:57.579
tasks that you shouldn't
be doing will really help.

00:11:57.579 --> 00:11:59.402
You want to spend as
much time in the CEO role

00:11:59.402 --> 00:12:01.828
as possible, that's where you want to be.

00:12:01.828 --> 00:12:04.005
So looking at your schedule
and seeing where am I spending

00:12:04.005 --> 00:12:05.912
time that should be
eliminated, what things can be

00:12:05.912 --> 00:12:08.324
automated and then whatever's
left that still has to get

00:12:08.324 --> 00:12:11.630
done how do I delegate
some of these other things

00:12:11.630 --> 00:12:13.999
so that I can focus on what I'm great at?

00:12:13.999 --> 00:12:15.943
So when I started my Youtube
channel, I did everything

00:12:15.943 --> 00:12:18.168
myself, I'm a big advocate
of not spending money

00:12:18.168 --> 00:12:20.195
to make money, don't go
and start hiring somebody

00:12:20.195 --> 00:12:22.139
if you're making zero with your business.

00:12:22.139 --> 00:12:23.730
But as soon as I started
making money on my Youtube

00:12:23.730 --> 00:12:26.052
channel, I was doing everything,
I was the camera man,

00:12:26.052 --> 00:12:27.555
I was the editor, I was the researcher,

00:12:27.555 --> 00:12:29.576
I was in front of the camera, everything.

00:12:29.576 --> 00:12:31.340
As soon I started making
money on my Youtube channel,

00:12:31.340 --> 00:12:33.877
I poured it back in and
the first person I hired

00:12:33.877 --> 00:12:35.001
was an editor.

00:12:35.001 --> 00:12:37.230
Because editing took me a
long time, I wasn't very good

00:12:37.230 --> 00:12:40.221
at it, I didn't want to get
good at it, more importantly.

00:12:40.221 --> 00:12:42.643
And then as I started making
more, I hired more people,

00:12:42.643 --> 00:12:45.567
more editors, the camera
man, I bought more gear,

00:12:45.567 --> 00:12:50.479
I got cameras, I got
microphones, I got researchers,

00:12:50.479 --> 00:12:51.907
I got people to help me
on the Youtube channel

00:12:51.907 --> 00:12:55.796
with the comments so my team
grew as my business grew

00:12:55.796 --> 00:12:58.020
but the thing that really
helps skyrocket the early

00:12:58.020 --> 00:13:00.277
growth was getting my first
editor so as soon as you can

00:13:00.277 --> 00:13:03.122
afford it bring in somebody
on to help alleviate

00:13:03.122 --> 00:13:05.491
some of the task that you're
not good and more importantly

00:13:05.491 --> 00:13:08.716
don't want to get at good
either can really help you

00:13:08.716 --> 00:13:11.894
quickly scale up your
business and reduce stress

00:13:11.894 --> 00:13:13.212
because you get most stressed out

00:13:13.212 --> 00:13:15.156
when you're doing work
that you don't want to do.

00:13:15.156 --> 00:13:17.751
So those are my seven ways
to effectively reduce stress.

00:13:17.751 --> 00:13:19.179
I'd love to know what did you think.

00:13:19.179 --> 00:13:21.350
Which way resonated the most with you.

00:13:21.350 --> 00:13:22.697
Do you have an eight,
nine, ten that you want

00:13:22.697 --> 00:13:25.309
to add to the list, leave it
down in the comments below,

00:13:25.309 --> 00:13:27.318
super curious to find
out what you have to say.

00:13:27.318 --> 00:13:29.325
I also want to give a quick
shout out to John Sonmez,

00:13:29.325 --> 00:13:32.053
thank you so much John for
picking up a copy of my book.

00:13:32.053 --> 00:13:33.819
I really really really appreciate it

00:13:33.819 --> 00:13:36.310
and if you're doing that
review, means a lot to me man

00:13:36.310 --> 00:13:37.825
and I'm glad you enjoyed the book.

00:13:37.825 --> 00:13:39.582
So thank you guys so much for watching,

00:13:39.582 --> 00:13:42.643
I believe in you, I hope you
continue to believe in yourself

00:13:42.643 --> 00:13:46.810
and whatever your one word is,
much love, I'll see you soon.

